WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.483
- I have a daughter who's three,

00:00:01.483 --> 00:00:03.209
and by the time she's having kids,

00:00:03.209 --> 00:00:05.916
I want the world to be
completely different for her.

00:00:05.916 --> 00:00:07.681
- So, should we go?

00:00:07.681 --> 00:00:08.750
Yay, let's go.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:09.583
Whoo.

00:00:13.474 --> 00:00:17.216
So many moms go through a postnatal mood

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.316
or anxiety disorder alone

00:00:19.316 --> 00:00:21.050
and don't know where to turn

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.657
and don't know where to look for help.

00:00:22.657 --> 00:00:24.261
And they know something's wrong,

00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:27.011
but they just lack the resources.

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:41.935
- When you're going through
postpartum depression,

00:00:41.935 --> 00:00:43.814
that's one of the most
isolating experiences

00:00:43.814 --> 00:00:45.142
that you can have.

00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:47.366
And I think, knowing that other people

00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:51.656
are going through it with you
is so incredibly important

00:00:51.656 --> 00:00:54.430
to being able to just keep breathing

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.860
and get out of bed everyday.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.684
- It wasn't until I
started talking about it

00:00:58.684 --> 00:01:00.932
and just having people I barely knew say,

00:01:00.932 --> 00:01:02.008
"Oh yeah, I had that."

00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:04.567
And then being able to
talk, that I just realized

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:07.977
I wasn't crazy, that I
hadn't done anything wrong.

00:01:07.977 --> 00:01:09.187
Unless you've walked
through that darkness,

00:01:09.187 --> 00:01:11.020
you just don't get it.

00:01:16.789 --> 00:01:17.781
- This is so common.

00:01:17.781 --> 00:01:20.759
They say one in seven moms go through this

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:22.207
but you wouldn't know it.

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:25.411
And we talk about
motherhood and giving birth

00:01:25.411 --> 00:01:28.745
as if it's this wonderful
joyous thing, and it is.

00:01:28.745 --> 00:01:31.602
But it can be very, very
difficult for a lot of moms.

00:01:31.602 --> 00:01:34.770
- My recovery didn't start
until I met other moms

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.272
who were going through
and had been through

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:38.441
the same experience as me.

00:01:38.441 --> 00:01:41.247
So every year, this is a great opportunity

00:01:41.247 --> 00:01:43.726
for other moms to come to a place

00:01:43.726 --> 00:01:45.350
where they're gonna find their community

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.032
and have that moment of recovery

00:01:47.032 --> 00:01:48.366
that I was so lucky to have.

00:01:48.366 --> 00:01:50.154
- [Voiceover] It's worth
it to get through it

00:01:50.154 --> 00:01:51.353
and connect with other people.

00:01:51.353 --> 00:01:52.711
- There's nothing more important

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:54.802
than knowing that you
are not the only person

00:01:54.802 --> 00:01:56.385
going through this.

00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:14.797
- It takes a team.

00:02:14.797 --> 00:02:16.563
We need every mother who has ever had

00:02:16.563 --> 00:02:18.512
maternal mental illness and every person

00:02:18.512 --> 00:02:20.904
who has ever loved someone
with a maternal mental illness

00:02:20.904 --> 00:02:22.716
to join our team.

00:02:22.716 --> 00:02:24.182
If we don't all come together,

00:02:24.182 --> 00:02:26.065
we'll never be able to get to the day

00:02:26.065 --> 00:02:28.456
when every mom knows what's wrong,

00:02:28.456 --> 00:02:30.379
knows where to go, gets help quickly,

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:32.240
and recovers quickly.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.612
If you are listening to this right now,

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:36.696
and you are a mom who is struggling,

00:02:36.696 --> 00:02:39.711
please know that you are
loved and understood.

00:02:39.711 --> 00:02:41.206
We know how you feel.

00:02:41.206 --> 00:02:45.991
We know all the doubts that
you have about yourself.

00:02:45.991 --> 00:02:47.402
We know what it's like to feel

00:02:47.402 --> 00:02:50.334
like you are a failure as a mother,

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:52.439
worried that you'll never get better.

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:54.182
We're also fortunate to have come out

00:02:54.182 --> 00:02:56.990
on the other side, so we know that you can

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.339
and will get through this.

00:02:58.339 --> 00:02:59.848
And we want you to know we will be here

00:02:59.848 --> 00:03:02.015
for you all along the way.

